{"skill":{"slug":"reflect-learn","displayName":"Reflect"},"version":{"version":"2.1.0","createdAt":1771297371403,"changelog":"Add Security category to signal detection, fix agent_mappings.md root-level agents, add Memory integration guidance, consistency fixes across reference files","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"CLAWDHUB-PUBLISHING-GUIDE.md","size":8460,"sha256":"aff3dc4753122943c86e5658c857f8f9c61638de4f2ea6c2003175b7e2527039","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":10682,"sha256":"aaf9bec12df53d3866d41c27349a23deafdf789e744f22d54967a8c1cc34d5d3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/learnings_schema.yaml","size":2680,"sha256":"c9965eb1ced98d45f8f06e22de878a717c714a2005367fd41d6bece8971a43c7","contentType":"text/yaml"},{"path":"assets/reflection_template.md","size":2014,"sha256":"0305f198da22db2928cedd04a6475c6ce4a7265cb07090c71c26166476fa1954","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"hooks/README.md","size":5951,"sha256":"bb0a924d9111a35aceb946d49b9b172e009fb3ab13e33ba5ed5dc09a8ebb7390","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"hooks/precompact_reflect.py","size":6847,"sha256":"31f8d6297d35ecd47879f8783d52e16a896edea5b2bc4443898775b01b90b55a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"hooks/settings-snippet.json","size":1108,"sha256":"7bf3a65cc05c2d0ced469d556849d387b4702b060cd2f05733308ee437c3543f","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"references/agent_mappings.md","size":7580,"sha256":"9be1a886e032e4169639ffb00b91e797bd93bf7c85a075bea45a0fc260963a0a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/signal_patterns.md","size":8427,"sha256":"34266d871b4266d3054660d5d3001f4b9ec385d519e87a46d6cf19360e1b71ee","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/skill_template.md","size":8771,"sha256":"cd5ce679e71b79e673c36b27432a928b98ccddc4f55ccc264ae5c73dc8b69724","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/logs/chat.json","size":1698179,"sha256":"88fc974c402d9d8b9f962dff3fbff4005b46be5660f4fadaaf1a8a04b9f3b2df","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/logs/notification.json","size":449,"sha256":"6fd137f0b9d6cfc6827ad06ee54dc07c41b01ccb5fc5184ec1d45837f25c59c3","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/logs/stop.json","size":425,"sha256":"09f7c295cc5b0b23f9f5301bac9eb215bf35efe1492d460db1073b373c373fbf","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/logs/subagent_stop.json","size":643,"sha256":"096cd76e2c2adf3918eb5fd6c14874ebf1478ec9848a54b3a36f74964a3ad49d","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/logs/user_prompt_submit.json","size":465,"sha256":"0674593631fd7d8b01c41742fdd09d15cac67289f2f49dfdc1cedb97ce8a5851","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/metrics_updater.py","size":8113,"sha256":"2bfe85729d0af3243635e8163a4bc7ae8f8569d18b16e7b3a035dcf3f69670b0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/output_generator.py","size":14763,"sha256":"856080683994685e80068f4a3e726625d772400cf013349938498a3c582f888b","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/signal_detector.py","size":11874,"sha256":"e829c0a831c628e23795fc293c06af7dc044444ac01bdd74c5b7b86de94da82d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/state_manager.py","size":6933,"sha256":"e69e248f7569d670b890f9b025797b25ec7fdf5763ced4f8ef21603a765556be","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2835,"sha256":"70f6d1ce0fe946b704a04ab365e2e97f02ef96f9dcd89be1ad10d3ff063094fb","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021820448,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"fa9984629e5a3960310efb62bf08cb8cebc8d7adb964dd11810e6363d3bda2bb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/fa9984629e5a3960310efb62bf08cb8cebc8d7adb964dd11810e6363d3bda2bb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: reflect-learn\nVersion: 2.1.0\n\nThe skill is designed for agent self-improvement, allowing it to analyze conversations, propose updates to its own configuration files, and create new skills. While this involves powerful capabilities like modifying agent files, creating new skill definitions, and using the `Bash` tool, the `SKILL.md` explicitly outlines strong safety guardrails, including mandatory human approval for all proposed changes, Git versioning for easy rollbacks, and incremental updates. The Python scripts handle file operations within expected `.claude/` and `~/.reflect/` directories, and there is no evidence of data exfiltration, unauthorized persistence, or malicious execution beyond the stated purpose. The instructions themselves do not contain prompt injection attempts to bypass security or hide actions.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160047585},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":361,"checkedAt":1789021820448},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill has a coherent self-improvement purpose, but it can persistently change agent instructions, install a cross-session hook, and includes private developer session logs, so it needs careful review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Project-level outputs are proportionate, but global writes under ~/.claude plus bundled real session logs and transcript metadata exceed what a portable reflection skill needs by default.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The hook installation is disclosed and manual, but it asks users to copy a script into ~/.claude/hooks and configure ~/.claude/settings.json so code can run on future PreCompact events.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The main instructions require explicit user approval and diffs before applying changes, but the references route learnings into global agent files and include broad language about always applying high-confidence learnings.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Cross-session persistence is central to the skill and disclosed, but the unvalidated skill creation path and optional persistent hook create high-impact agent-behavior modification risk.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches reflection and learning, but the capability surface includes persistent edits to agent files, new skill creation, memory files, metrics, global reflection indexes, and optional hook execution.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intentionally want a skill that can propose and apply persistent changes to agent instructions and create new skills. Keep auto-reflection hooks disabled until you review the hook script and settings snippet, require explicit approval before any edits, remove the bundled logs from the package, validate skill names before file creation, and pin hook dependencies.","findings":"[RA1] expected: The publishing-guide 'Update SKILL.md' item is documentation, not runtime self-modification; persistent agent and skill updates are part of the stated purpose but remain high-impact.\n[TP4] expected: The frontmatter does disclose agent-file updates and new skill creation, and SKILL.md later discloses hooks; the concern is under-scoping of broad persistent authority, not hidden unrelated behavior.\n[AS1] expected: References to ~/.claude/settings.json, ~/.claude/session, and ~/.claude hooks are for state and optional integration, not credential harvesting, but they affect sensitive agent configuration.\n[LP1] expected: The use of /usr/bin/env and REFLECT_STATE_DIR is consistent with the script mechanism and documented configuration; I did not treat this as deceptive on its own.\n[YR4] unexpected: The match appears to come from bundled chat transcript content and tool metadata rather than active offensive functionality; it supports a packaging/privacy concern instead.\n[T09] unexpected: scripts/output_generator.py creates .claude/skills/{skill_name}/SKILL.md without validating skill_name, so traversal or absolute paths could write SKILL.md outside the intended directory.\n[T09] unexpected: scripts/logs/chat.json and related logs include real session IDs, absolute local paths, tool outputs, permission metadata, and assistant reasoning; these are not needed for the installed skill.\n[T08] expected: The PreCompact hook uses an unpinned pyyaml dependency through uv and the publishing guide suggests an unpinned global npm install; this is supply-chain hygiene risk rather than evidence of malicious code.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021820448}}}}}